What These Specific Classes Are

Because the APK has been minified with R8/ProGuard, standard Android framework and Jetpack support libraries have been renamed to short obfuscated identifiers (LN/U;, LV0/c;, etc.). You can identify them directly from their log strings:
• LN/U;->e() (androidx.core.view.WindowInsetsCompat): Standard AndroidX compatibility code checking via reflection if WindowInsets.CONSUMED exists on older Android versions.
• LV0/c;->e() (androidx.loader.app.LoaderManagerImpl): Standard dump() method used by Android's dumpsys utility to print loader states (Loaders:, mId=, mStarted=) during system diagnostics.
• LM3/h;->f() & LT4/a;->g() (Firebase Crashlytics / Analytics): Standard SDK initialization messages registering breadcrumb receivers.
• LM3/c;->c(), LM4/a;->run(), LS3/f;->b(), LU4/b;->c(): Standard exception handling and debug logging calls inside minified SDKs.

Recommended Next Steps

Since trueseeing prints every low{tentative} log call in alphabetical order across thousands of classes, reading the raw terminal stream line-by-line will mostly show R8-minified Jetpack and Google Play Services code.
• Save the full scan to a file first so you don't have to scroll through terminal output:bash
trueseeing -eQc "s;gt" betPawa.apk > scan_results.txt
Use code with caution.
